From 0edc4a53353ef39324351e2ee2184cb290eaa68e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:07:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Hunters' Rumours, the guild hunters and Guild Scribe
 Verity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Hunters' Rumours were not implemented: the Hunter Guild's
hunters and Verity had no dialogue and catches gave no rare parts.

Change. Rumour state in server varps (63772-63783): one rumour per
guild hunter, the current hunter, the pity count. Assignment follows
each hunter's list, the unboostable Hunter level, the rumour's quest
(Eagles' Peak for the chinchompa and jerboa rumours, Bone Voyage and 31
Herblore for the herbiboar, through QuestRequirements) and no duplicate
across hunters. Catches of the current creature (box traps, bird
snares, the herbiboar harvest, butterflies and moths) roll the rare part
with the wiki's rates and pity thresholds (a held part blocks, a full
inventory drops a rolled part and destroys a pity part). Turn-in gives
(level + 5) * 50/55/60 XP and the tier's loot sack; the quetzal
whistle's Rumour op names the target; ::rumour for testing. The Burrow's
guild hunters (Gilman, Cervus, Ornus, Aco, Teco, Wolf) and Verity follow
the wiki transcripts: Talk-to and the Rumour op assign, remind, switch
and hand in (the turn-in lines RuneLite's Hunter Rumours plugin tracks);
each line says "one of its", "some of its" or "its" as its transcript
does; "No." to another rumour goes back to the hunter's options; Wolf's
"Never mind." option has the player say "See you later.". Verity
unlocks rumours, counts them and toggles back-to-back rumours. Gilman
sells Trapper's Tipple and stew. Server-only dbtables
hunter_rumour_hunters (56010) and hunter_rumours (56011; quest and
Herblore columns), rows 60271-60280 and 60288-60293, own
HunterRumourPluginPack. Needs the bird snare/box trap, Herbiboar and
butterfly commits (their catches report to the rumours).

Tests. Integration suites HunterRumoursTest (7: turn-in XP, assignment
rules, quest and Herblore requirements, pity and the whistle, a pity part
on a full inventory, turn-in once), HunterGuildScriptTest (5: the
"one of / some of / its" lines, Wolf's leave option, Gilman's stew),
ButterflyScriptTest's rumour catch.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki: Hunters' Rumours (list of rumours and its
notes, rates and pity, turn-in XP, rules), Basic quetzal whistle,
Goat hunting ("one of its hooves"), Transcript: Huntmaster Gilman
(Novice), Guild Hunter Cervus/Ornus (Adept), Aco/Teco (Expert), Wolf
(Master), Guild Scribe Verity. Quest keys quest_eaglespeak and
quest_bonevoyage are the cache dbrows.

Caveats. Under the default assume-completed quest mode the quest
requirements count as met. Guesses: wagtail and herbiboar part wordings,
the pity reset on a new rumour, the part rolling on Check, the
no-rumour whistle message, the level line for hunters other than Wolf,
the nothing-to-offer line, Gilman's Yes/No switch without an old rumour,
the back-to-back rule. Not done: guild hunter outfit pity, loot sacks
opening, milestone unlocks, Wolf's At First Light requirement, Verity's
spare-gear trade, the "intel reshuffle" lines, rumours for creatures the
server can't catch.

